Fixed #1126 and committed as f61f588b. An ordinary DNS failure now ends with the 💡 network hint. Before this fix it retried six times and stopped without one. fmt, clippy -D warnings, build and the full cargo test run all pass.

The cause: diagnose_api_error only looked for "dns resolution failed" and "name resolution failed". The real reqwest error (ConnectError("dns error", … "failed to lookup address information: Name or service not known")) contains neither, so the hint never fired.

The fix is in src/prompt_retry.rs. The network branch now also matches:
• "dns error"
• "failed to lookup address information" (the wording on Linux and macOS)
• "name resolution", widened from "name resolution failed" so Temporary failure in name resolution (a temporary resolver failure on Linux) matches too

The hint goes out through the same branch as before, so -p still drops the REPL-only /retry line.

Checked on the built binary with --base-url http://no-such-host-yoyo-probe-4821.com -p hi:
• Before: (failed after 6 attempts) and no 💡 line.
• After: 💡 Network error — could not reach the API.

Tests are in a new file, src/prompt_retry_dns_tests.rs:
• They reuse the captured REAL error text rather than retyping it, and compare the whole hint string.
• There are rows for the macOS and temporary-failure wordings and for both old spellings.
• Two near-misses: Connection refused gets the same hint as before, byte for byte, and image resolution too large gets no network hint.
• The old test_diagnose_dns_resolution_failed test is untouched.

As a positive control, I disabled the three new matches (marked NEUTERED) and restored them in one command. The two real-text tests failed by name, then all three passed after the restore.

Reserved names (.invalid, .test, …) still stop early through reserved_dns before any hint is printed, so there is no duplicate, and the reserved_dns tests still pass.

To share REAL, I moved it out of reserved_dns's test module into a test-only pub(crate) const. I also changed mod reserved_dns to pub(crate) in src/prompt.rs, which wasn't in the task's file list. Neither change touches any logic.

prompt_retry.rs grew from 2787 to 2793 lines, and I updated its entry in tests/module_size.rs with a comment naming #1126. The troubleshooting doc didn't need changing: it says non-reserved DNS failures keep the normal retries, which is still true. The wording of the billing and model hints (#1128) was out of scope and is unchanged.

